    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Rest and motion are relative states depending on the chosen frame of reference.",
        "Distance measures total path length (scalar), while displacement is the shortest path between initial and final points (vector).",
        "Acceleration measures the rate of change of velocity with respect to time.",
        "The three standard equations of motion apply specifically to uniformly accelerated straight-line motion."
